#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# robust_convex_optimization

#% text
# `robust_convex_optimization(f, for_all(params, region, cons), vars)` gives the point that minimizes `f` such that the constraints `cons` hold for every value of the uncertain parameters in `region`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The region must be a box: bounds on each parameter, written as inequalities or as `element(p, interval([lo, hi]))`. With constraints affine in the parameters the worst cases are the corners of the box, so the problem is solved with the constraints at all corners.

#% item
# Other regions (a ball, a polytope) leave the call unevaluated.

#% item
# A fourth argument selects the result as for `quadratic_optimization`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
robust_convex_optimization(x + y, for_all([a, b], -1 <= a and a <= 1 and 0 <= b and b <= 1, 10*x >= a and y >= b), [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 1/10, y -> 1]

#% cell
robust_convex_optimization(x + y, for_all(t, -1 <= t and t <= 1, [x + 2*y >= 3 + t, x >= -1]), [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> -1, y -> 5/2]

#% cell
robust_convex_optimization(x + y, for_all(t, element(t, interval([-1, 1])), [x + 2*y >= 3 + t, x >= -1]), [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> -1, y -> 5/2]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `parametric_convex_optimization`, `convex_optimization`, `for_all`
